.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBTabs\fR: a row of tabs and the panel of the active one, after Mantine's Tabs and Radix UI's. The behavior (which tab a click activates, disabled tabs) is the \fBtabs\fR primitive, shared with the segmented control behind \fBtoggle_group\fR.
.PP
A tab can be \fBclosable\fR: the close button is drawn in the style of the variant and sends the tab's key to \fBon_close\fR (the app removes it).
.PP
Controlled: the app owns the active key and takes it from \fBon_change\fR. Each tab may carry the panel that shows while it is active (built only then), or none, for a list that drives something else (the gallery's Preview / Code tabs).
.PP
.nf
.RS
Tabs::new(Some(self.tab), Msg::Tab)
    .variant(TabsVariant::Floating)
    .tab(TabItem::new(Tab::Gallery, "Gallery").icon(Icon::Home).panel(|| gallery()))
    .tab(TabItem::new(Tab::Messages, "Messages").panel(|| messages()))
    .tab(TabItem::new(Tab::Settings, "Settings").disabled(true))
.RE
.fi
.PP
Variants, as in Mantine: \fBDefault\fR (an accent line under the active tab, over a hairline), \fBOutline\fR (the active tab boxed), \fBPills\fR (the active tab filled) and \fBFloating\fR (a highlight that slides behind the active tab, a \fBFloatingIndicator\fR). Arrow\-key navigation is not included: iced has no focus model to hang it on (the primitive has \fBstep\fR for it).
